WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.880
The sheer scale of the refugee crisis in Bangladesh.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:10.780
Hundreds of thousands of Rohinga Muslims are
living in squalid camps - just like this.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.849
They've fled Myanmar because of army-led violence
following a military crackdown.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:21.980
But with agreement from Myanmar, today Bangladesh
begins the enormous task of trying to repatriate

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.369
them.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.420
It's a move that is proving deeply unpopular.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.679
"The Rohingya community leader told me that
my number has been listed and I have to return

00:00:33.679 --> 00:00:34.969
to Myanmar.

00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:37.100
But my son and daughter were killed there.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.899
I cannot pray there.

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:41.250
No one talks about our rights there.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.549
We were sent away after being labelled as
'Bengali.'

00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:47.120
We will not go back there."

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.699
This family have fled the Bangladeshi camp
they called their home and are in hiding - so

00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:54.420
fearful are they of returning to Myanmar.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:01.279
They have tortured us so much, there are no
words to explain it.

00:01:01.279 --> 00:01:05.460
We went through so much pain and if we go
back again to face the same, then why should

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.460
we go?

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.479
It is better to die here by taking poison.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:10.790
There, we will have to stay in camps.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.290
We are already in camps here, so it is better
to die here.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:18.909
I feel that I will die here, so don't try
to send us there."

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:24.060
Aid organisations and the UN refugee agency
admit there are still concerns for the safety

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.960
of those who do return.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.391
But nervertheless the work to repatriate 150
Rohinga a day is underway.

00:01:30.391 --> 00:01:32.079
Bangladesh`s Refugees, Repatriation and Rehabilitation
Commissioner

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:36.289
"We are still talking to the Rohingya refugees.

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:39.820
Our people are working on the ground to encourage
them to go back.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.969
Our associated organisations are also working."

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.950
Life in camps like this is far from easy.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:52.479
But for many Rohinga staying here is far better
than being forced to return back home.

